# Large media assets — too big for git, served from /var/www directly.
# If you reinstall the server from scratch, these need to be restored
# manually (look in backups, or re-export from local copies).
demo.mp4
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm

# The installers are NOT canonical here. The source of truth for every one of
# them lives in github.com/pensados/sentinelx-cloud-installer. They get
# copied into this directory at deploy time so nginx can serve them at
# https://get.sentinelx.app/<file>.
#
# Tracking them here would mean two sources of truth that can drift -- and it
# did: install.ps1 and install-macos.sh were tracked here too, a 2026-09-21
# change to install.ps1 was committed here instead of there, and the
# canonical copy fell behind the served one. Always edit them in
# sentinelx-cloud-installer, then sync over.
install.sh
enroll.py
install.ps1
install-macos.sh
dispatch.sh

# Editor backups (sentinel_edit leaves these on failed transactions)
*.bak.*
*.bak

# OS clutter
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor scratch
*.swp
*~
